<title>SWITZERLAND: Oelikon-Buehrle unit sells spinning plant.</title>
<headline>Oelikon-Buehrle unit sells spinning plant.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spinnerei Kunz AG, a subsidiary of Swiss conglomerate Oerlikon-Buehrle Holding AG, said it will sell some cotton spinning operations based in Linthal, Switzerland, on June 1, 1997.</p>
<p>No price for the transaction was disclosed.</p>
<p>The spinning operations will be sold to European textile firms Hacontex AG of Zollikon, and cotton concern Niggeler &amp; Kuepfer SpA of Brescia, Kunz said.</p>
<p>The two firms already cooperate in sales and production.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial, +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
